the white house confirms senior u.s  diplomats will boycott february's winter  olympics in beijing american athletes  will still participate but the move is a  high-profile protest over china's human  rights record  elizabeth palmer is in south korea  that's home of the last winter games  with the issues that the china's olympic  organizers are now facing  china has been spending billions on  state-of-the-art venues for what it  hoped would be a lavish and prestigious  olympics so this announcement comes as a  blow  the biden administration will not send  any diplomatic or official  representation to the beijing 2022  winter olympics and paralympic games  given the pierre scenes ongoing genocide  and crimes against  humanity and xinjiang and other human  rights abuses beijing's brand new  facilities were going to be empty of  foreign spectators anyway thanks to  kovid but the white house's decision has  infuriated the chinese  china's foreign affairs spokesman  replied with a warning  the u.s will pay a price for its  practices  you may stay tuned for follow-ups  in spite of a phone summit between  president biden and china's president xi  jinping last month relations remain  pretty frosty  the fact that the u.s is using the  boycott to highlight china's treatment  of the muslim uyghur people in its  xinjiang province  is bound to deepen the chill  six times in olympic history boycotts  have tarnished the games  two of the most famous were in 1980 when  the u.s and 65 other countries stayed  away from the moscow olympics after the  soviet invasion of afghanistan  four years later the soviets and their  allies retaliated boycotting the games  in l.a  as one of the key players who made sure  the 2018 winter games in pyeongchang  south korea went off with no political  hitches  governor moon soon choi told me the u.s  boycott will have a huge impact how much  of it is will be a blow to the way the  beijing olympics  are remembered in history  if the u.s delegation doesn't go to  beijing he said those games will not be  considered a success  so far the us is going it alone in this  human rights-based diplomatic boycott of  the beijing games the australians have  also said that they're not going to send  any officials but they claim that it was  a decision made  some time ago and it has to do with  covid security vlad  all right elizabeth palmer reporting  from south korea liz thank you as always
 

